WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:39.790
The International Olympic Committee has the honour of announcing that the

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:46.298
21st Olympic Winter Games in 2010 are awarded to the city of

00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:48.061
Vancouver.

00:00:58.659 --> 00:00:59.701
This is my perfect city,

00:01:00.201 --> 00:01:00.640
Vancouver,

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.161
Canada.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:20.383
Vancouver has been chosen by an influential British magazine as the world's most livable city.

00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:24.344
Vancouver has come out on top in a survey of 130 cities around the world.

00:01:24.344 --> 00:01:27.829
It's really not hard to see why Vancouver is considered one of the best.

00:01:27.844 --> 00:01:31.350
This is the fifth year in a row that Vancouver has topped this list.

00:01:31.647 --> 00:01:35.154
But take one wrong turn and you're in the roughest area in North America.

00:01:35.608 --> 00:01:37.355
Vancouver's downtown east side guest.

00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:42.459
I just got a bottle broken over my head.

00:01:44.847 --> 00:01:45.609
Who the fuck threw that?

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:51.111
As I was saying,

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.933
this is the roughest neighborhood in North America.

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:55.935
One out of every three homeless people living here have AIDS.

00:01:56.172 --> 00:01:57.396
Two out of three people have Hep C.

00:01:57.412 --> 00:02:00.798
It has the highest crime rate per capita in North America.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.020
Living conditions are on par with Botswana,

00:02:03.154 --> 00:02:03.660
Africa,

00:02:03.954 --> 00:02:04.901
a third world country.

00:02:05.514 --> 00:02:08.503
How can this place be known as the best city in the world?

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:20.596
The disparity between this neighborhood and Vancouver's reputation as one of the world's most livable cities is disturbing.

00:02:21.536 --> 00:02:24.737
We have this horrible secret that is the Downtown Eastside.

00:02:26.318 --> 00:02:29.500
The most concentrated area of drug use in all of North America.

00:02:31.159 --> 00:02:37.902
Many people aren't aware that this community experienced the most explosive HIV epidemic ever seen in the developed world.

00:02:39.956 --> 00:02:40.456
Alcohol,

00:02:40.497 --> 00:02:40.997
drugs,

00:02:41.198 --> 00:02:41.638
HIV,

00:02:41.638 --> 00:02:42.320
hepatitis C,

00:02:42.539 --> 00:02:44.764
in the last decade that's what we're seeing a lot of.

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:50.433
How as a society did we get into this situation in the first place?

00:02:54.611 --> 00:02:55.431
In all this mess,

00:02:56.012 --> 00:02:57.252
what am I doing to help my city?

00:02:58.012 --> 00:02:58.512
Well,

00:02:59.173 --> 00:02:59.712
I wake up,

00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:00.933
I sing,

00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:02.013
I study,

00:03:02.613 --> 00:03:03.293
and I stress.

00:03:04.074 --> 00:03:05.254
But I don't make a difference.

00:03:06.174 --> 00:03:08.555
Sure,
sometimes I talk about the issues with friends at school,

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.596
padding my academic ego with stats from the morning's paper.

00:03:12.176 --> 00:03:12.656
But,

00:03:12.656 --> 00:03:13.257
as always,

00:03:13.616 --> 00:03:15.557
that frail state of caring dissipates.

00:03:15.877 --> 00:03:16.858
Gotta go back to class,

00:03:17.177 --> 00:03:17.677
lunch,

00:03:17.858 --> 00:03:18.358
nap,

00:03:18.578 --> 00:03:19.078
dinner,

00:03:19.358 --> 00:03:19.858
movie,

00:03:20.218 --> 00:03:20.718
sleep.

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:22.039
It's all so familiar.

00:03:23.223 --> 00:03:24.890
But one day everything changed.

00:03:25.956 --> 00:03:27.557
While having lunch with a friend on the force,

00:03:28.057 --> 00:03:29.778
I presented my opinion on homelessness.

00:03:30.278 --> 00:03:31.338
Living on the streets is easy.

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:32.560
They don't want to work.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.980
They're a bunch of scammers.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.902
They can get a job like everybody else and work a nine-to-five.

00:03:36.903 --> 00:03:37.861
They don't want to do that.

00:03:38.423 --> 00:03:41.004
They got everything they need just living there on the street.

00:03:41.064 --> 00:03:41.584
You got no idea,

00:03:41.604 --> 00:03:42.104
man.

00:03:42.564 --> 00:03:43.306
I say,
what you want to do?

00:03:43.846 --> 00:03:44.986
Go down there for 30 days?

00:03:45.807 --> 00:03:46.427
All my friends say,

00:03:46.427 --> 00:03:47.707
I want to go on some crazy vacation.

00:03:47.709 --> 00:03:48.348
I say,
you know what?

00:03:48.348 --> 00:03:49.248
Go get a room down there,

00:03:49.468 --> 00:03:50.468
and then we'll see what it's all about.

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:52.050
She went on about the gang wars,

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.211
drug busts,

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.010
shootings,

00:03:54.471 --> 00:03:55.312
but I wasn't listening.

00:03:56.072 --> 00:03:57.513
All I could hear was one tiny,

00:03:57.772 --> 00:03:58.573
horrible word.

00:03:59.153 --> 00:03:59.653
Go.

00:03:59.813 --> 00:04:00.593
I couldn't shake it.

00:04:00.715 --> 00:04:01.215
School,

00:04:01.235 --> 00:04:01.655
work,

00:04:01.655 --> 00:04:02.134
rent,

00:04:02.134 --> 00:04:02.635
get HIV,

00:04:03.036 --> 00:04:03.436
shot,

00:04:03.436 --> 00:04:03.855
stabbed.

00:04:03.855 --> 00:04:04.355
Go.

00:04:07.918 --> 00:04:09.359
By the time the beer hit my lips,

00:04:10.038 --> 00:04:10.840
it was decided.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.140
For 31 days in December,

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.722
I will conduct a social experiment on myself.

00:04:16.202 --> 00:04:21.004
I will totally abandon my predictable life and attempt to survive the streets of Vancouver.
do you know where there's any place where I can get food and shelter around here?

00:04:21.004 --> 00:04:22.406
Leaving behind my possessions,

00:04:22.646 --> 00:04:23.326
I...
identity,

00:04:23.466 --> 00:04:24.266
friends,
and family.

00:04:24.947 --> 00:04:27.709
My goal is to confront the challenges of street life firsthand,

00:04:28.286 --> 00:04:29.651
so I see how hard it really is.

00:04:30.648 --> 00:04:31.452
This experiment,

00:04:31.788 --> 00:04:32.288
I hope,

00:04:32.288 --> 00:04:35.196
will shed light on a crisis that is spiraling out of control.

00:04:35.769 --> 00:04:36.276
And well,

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.379
instead of crossing a bridge downtown,

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:39.238
I'm swimming,

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.321
so I start my journey freezing,

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.091
wet,

00:04:42.091 --> 00:04:42.661
and naked.

00:05:09.784 --> 00:05:13.593
I arrived downtown with nothing but a backpack with a hidden video camera inside.

00:05:16.028 --> 00:05:17.702
The temperature was around the freezing mark,

00:05:18.069 --> 00:05:19.446
but thankfully the rain stopped.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:23.432
My first challenge was to find city services offering food,

00:05:23.566 --> 00:05:24.473
shelter and clothing.

00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:26.634
I had no idea where to look,

00:05:27.069 --> 00:05:28.871
so I went to Granville Street to ask the locals.

00:05:30.212 --> 00:05:30.977
Someone had to know.

00:05:30.978 --> 00:05:35.260
Hey you guys,
do you guys know a place right here where I can get some free food and shelter?

00:05:36.676 --> 00:05:38.077
Know where I can get some free food and shelter?

00:05:40.418 --> 00:05:40.918
No idea.
0:05:41.679,0:04:19.960
Hey man,

00:05:45.182 --> 00:05:46.141
Well there's a gallery there,
it's just two blocks.

00:05:47.187 --> 00:05:47.703
Two blocks down?

00:05:47.703 --> 00:05:48.464
Thanks a lot man.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:50.484
Enter the Gathering Place,

00:05:50.924 --> 00:05:52.393
a resource centre for the homeless.

00:05:52.945 --> 00:05:53.935
When I walked through the door,

00:05:54.266 --> 00:05:56.938
they told me I was hypothermic and threw me into a hot shower.

00:05:58.764 --> 00:06:02.328
They gave me some clothes and told me to go talk to the guy at the front counter when I was done.

00:06:03.146 --> 00:06:04.608
So,
tell me everything I get.

00:06:04.608 --> 00:06:09.971
You get everything that we do at the place.

00:06:09.971 --> 00:06:11.278
So you get to go to the laundry rooms,

00:06:11.491 --> 00:06:11.852
the pool rooms,

00:06:11.852 --> 00:06:12.273
the video game rooms,

00:06:12.273 --> 00:06:12.733
the showers,

00:06:12.733 --> 00:06:14.837
the...
Clothing donation area,

00:06:14.838 --> 00:06:15.637
jacuzzi,

00:06:15.637 --> 00:06:16.537
we're on fitness classes.

00:06:17.277 --> 00:06:17.918
What about yoga?

00:06:18.198 --> 00:06:18.818
Do I get yoga?

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.819
