Whenever I want free clothes,

00:12:02.409 --> 00:12:02.969
I go get them.

00:12:03.357 --> 00:12:04.578
Whenever I want free food,

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:05.459
I go to the charities.

00:12:05.811 --> 00:12:06.191
You know,

00:12:06.191 --> 00:12:07.400
I even ride the bus for free.

00:12:07.941 --> 00:12:08.581
Just get on,

00:12:08.801 --> 00:12:09.562
say I have no money.

00:12:10.002 --> 00:12:10.514
It's easy.

00:12:11.335 --> 00:12:15.347
Now the thing I don't get is why a lot of the homeless don't use these free services on the regular.

00:12:15.918 --> 00:12:17.259
Why make life so hard on yourself?

00:12:18.219 --> 00:12:18.729
I don't know.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.481
But maybe if I make life a bit harder on myself,

00:12:21.561 --> 00:12:22.781
I'll find the answer.

00:12:23.631 --> 00:12:25.071
So no more bubble baths.

00:12:25.652 --> 00:12:27.212
It's time to make money the hard way,

00:12:27.663 --> 00:12:28.612
by working for it.

00:12:29.204 --> 00:12:29.713
Besides,

00:12:29.784 --> 00:12:30.825
my welfare check's spent.

00:12:31.413 --> 00:12:33.386
And the boys say the big money's in squeegeeing.

00:12:33.906 --> 00:12:35.274
So I stole one and got to work.

00:12:42.696 --> 00:12:43.510
Although profitable,

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.137
squeegeeing was abusive,

00:12:45.357 --> 00:12:45.831
dangerous,

00:12:45.831 --> 00:12:46.471
and demeaning.

00:12:47.011 --> 00:12:48.318
So I thought I'd try panhandling.

00:13:04.125 --> 00:13:04.731
Panhandling

00:13:04.745 --> 00:13:05.411
wasn't my gig.

00:13:06.166 --> 00:13:07.213
I didn't make that much money.

00:13:07.567 --> 00:13:09.088
Plus it was boring and cold.

00:13:09.848 --> 00:13:11.656
So why not search for empties in the city's bins?

00:13:12.336 --> 00:13:12.857
After all,

00:13:13.451 --> 00:13:16.059
one man's garbage can be another man's pleasure.

00:13:16.173 --> 00:13:17.154
I need some privacy.

00:13:17.634 --> 00:13:19.016
Camera person,

00:13:19.017 --> 00:13:26.788
turn it off.

00:13:26.788 --> 00:13:28.769
I got cut up and stinky for low pay.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:30.910
You rifle through dog crap,

00:13:31.265 --> 00:13:31.770
vomit,

00:13:31.865 --> 00:13:32.691
use condoms,

00:13:33.086 --> 00:13:34.566
trying to find anything of value.

00:13:35.092 --> 00:13:37.032
Get pricked by a disease needle and you're dead.

00:13:37.848 --> 00:13:39.573
I asked Brian how he felt about binning.

00:13:39.973 --> 00:13:41.549
He showed me there's dignity in it.

00:13:42.394 --> 00:13:43.774
This is probably some lifesaver for me.

00:13:50.197 --> 00:13:50.776
Is this a saver for me?

00:13:50.776 --> 00:13:51.519
Yeah,
it really is.

00:13:51.559 --> 00:13:53.057
I know that sounds retarded to the average guy.

00:13:53.057 --> 00:13:53.617
I don't need to do this job.

00:13:54.524 --> 00:13:54.844
But for now...

00:13:54.844 --> 00:13:56.226
I'm going to make a lot of shots.

00:13:57.768 --> 00:13:58.950
But for now,

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.194
This is probably all fake.

00:14:01.194 --> 00:14:01.555
Yeah,

00:14:01.555 --> 00:14:02.404
it really is.

00:14:02.865 --> 00:14:04.685
Whether the public knows it or not,

00:14:05.846 --> 00:14:07.987
this is saving the public big money.

00:14:08.205 --> 00:14:10.688
Because it costs like 80 grand to keep a guy in prison.

00:14:11.428 --> 00:14:12.208
A guy's not,

00:14:12.209 --> 00:14:13.189
he can't do this.

00:14:13.269 --> 00:14:14.791
Like,
if he takes the bottles away,

00:14:14.911 --> 00:14:17.373
he costs the alleys or whatever.

00:14:17.392 --> 00:14:18.453
Yeah.

00:14:19.315 --> 00:14:20.236
it's a lot of work.

00:14:20.894 --> 00:14:22.374
Yeah,
like if you figure out the money.

00:14:22.374 --> 00:14:23.475
I've been out for 11 years.

00:14:23.475 --> 00:14:24.878
Since 97 I got out.

00:14:25.436 --> 00:14:26.600
So,

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:29.103
if you figure out the amount of money that I've saved...

00:14:29.143 --> 00:14:29.825
Basically by spending.

00:14:29.825 --> 00:14:30.278
It's saving the government.

00:14:30.278 --> 00:14:30.766
It really is.

00:14:30.766 --> 00:14:31.486
If you recycle,

00:14:31.506 --> 00:14:33.068
88...

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:34.239
88 million?

00:14:34.239 --> 00:14:34.880
88 million.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:38.441
Yeah.

00:14:39.417 --> 00:14:41.262
And that's been hanging up here since I've been here.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:45.965
This bottle depot was founded by a binner and serves only downtown Eastside residents.

00:14:46.546 --> 00:14:47.146
And believe me,

00:14:47.265 --> 00:14:48.108
it gets used.

00:14:48.745 --> 00:14:50.486
It generates $2 million a year for the binners.

00:14:52.593 --> 00:14:53.815
One morning's worth of recycling.

00:15:12.949 --> 00:15:14.370
With the little money I made binning,

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:15.920
I decided to treat myself.

00:15:16.761 --> 00:15:17.742
Double Big Mac meal,

00:15:18.092 --> 00:15:18.763
supersized.

00:15:19.133 --> 00:15:21.025
Six McNuggets and a large hot chocolate.

00:15:21.595 --> 00:15:24.797
And that's when I met Captain Tone.

00:15:37.642 --> 00:15:38.142
Sir,

00:15:38.302 --> 00:15:40.505
you're going to my machine.

00:15:40.506 --> 00:15:41.607
I can't do that.

00:15:41.627 --> 00:15:42.705
not no more.

00:15:42.705 --> 00:15:43.089
Close the door.

00:15:43.089 --> 00:15:43.890
It's cold.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:44.230
buddy.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:45.912
Close the door.

00:15:46.052 --> 00:15:47.214
You're fucking...

00:15:47.215 --> 00:15:49.317
You're not going to get a thing.

00:15:58.161 --> 00:16:03.384
Can you close the door?

00:16:03.384 --> 00:16:03.743
No.

00:16:03.743 --> 00:16:05.064
Hey Get out of here.

00:16:05.084 --> 00:16:12.150
You have to do this.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:16.611
Well,
I think Vancouver is an interesting but disturbing social experiment.

00:16:17.169 --> 00:16:25.696
Policymakers convinced many people working with the mentally ill that they would take the mentally ill out of institutions like Riverview.

00:16:28.915 --> 00:16:29.916
In 2005,

00:16:30.497 --> 00:16:30.997
Riverview,

00:16:31.759 --> 00:16:33.961
one of the largest mental hospitals in North America,

00:16:34.502 --> 00:16:37.526
transferred thousands of patients into downtown Vancouver.

00:16:39.957 --> 00:16:41.658
Expected to be more independent,

00:16:42.138 --> 00:16:44.339
the mentally ill would go unsupervised,

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:46.361
live in a more home-like setting,

00:16:46.761 --> 00:16:48.102
and become part of the community,

00:16:48.662 --> 00:16:49.783
like a normal citizen.

00:16:50.403 --> 00:16:51.243
Unfortunately,

00:16:51.664 --> 00:16:53.665
they were basically left to fend for themselves.

00:16:53.685 --> 00:16:55.406
The community supports weren't there.

00:16:56.066 --> 00:17:01.509
The community mental health agencies were overrun and understaffed and inability to meet demand.

00:17:01.969 --> 00:17:03.750
And people ended up coming here,

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:05.391
just like people always have,

00:17:05.731 --> 00:17:06.592
to find cheap,

00:17:06.772 --> 00:17:07.853
affordable housing.

00:17:13.497 --> 00:17:14.978
When I returned to the Yukon shelter,

00:17:15.298 --> 00:17:16.439
they told me my time was up.

00:17:16.939 --> 00:17:19.841
They sent me away with a list of other emergency shelters.

00:17:20.562 --> 00:17:22.963
I had no idea what I was in for.

00:17:23.364 --> 00:17:24.584
If you want to pick ten things that determine why people are healthy or unhealthy...

00:17:28.447 --> 00:17:28.767
Well,

00:17:28.767 --> 00:17:31.229
housing makes the list every single time.

00:17:31.549 --> 00:17:36.713
And the housing that is available to most people living in poverty is completely substandard.

00:17:36.851 --> 00:17:43.057
You know,
when you have a large number of people sharing a single space and you have this increased prevalence of infectious diseases,

00:17:43.715 --> 00:17:45.699
it is a risky place for some people.

00:17:45.816 --> 00:17:47.340
And that's what we see in the hospital.

00:17:47.657 --> 00:17:50.422
People are getting infections in their skin and their legs,

00:17:50.538 --> 00:17:51.422
also pneumonia,

00:17:51.959 --> 00:17:52.943
gastroenteritis.

00:18:00.534 --> 00:18:01.155
Bed 40?

00:18:01.155 --> 00:18:01.655
no,

00:18:02.295 --> 00:18:02.996
Shit.

00:18:02.996 --> 00:18:03.496
Bed 50.

00:18:03.976 --> 00:18:04.477
Okay.

00:18:04.997 --> 00:18:10.081
You guys have to get your beds straight up here.

00:18:10.081 --> 00:18:11.242
Alright.
Okay.

00:18:14.162 --> 00:18:15.085
From down the hallway,

00:18:15.563 --> 00:18:18.908
I hear a symphony of horking phlegm and blaring rock and roll.

00:18:21.106 --> 00:18:24.752
The smell of fermenting feet and bed bug pesticide made me gag.

00:18:26.497 --> 00:18:28.498
Guys were vomiting in the bathroom sinks.

00:18:30.239 --> 00:18:32.541
The lineup was 30 minutes long to use the washroom.

00:18:34.562 --> 00:18:36.283
How on earth could anyone sleep in here?

00:18:44.968 --> 00:18:47.330
I can see why a lot of the homeless prefer to sleep outside.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.071
Some hear the stink,

00:18:49.591 --> 00:18:50.392
others the snoring.

00:18:50.972 --> 00:18:51.852
For me it's the phlegm.

00:18:52.853 --> 00:18:56.117
The guy in the bed next to mine spat mouthfuls onto the floor all night.

00:18:56.795 --> 00:18:58.219
It was absolute torture.

00:18:59.457 --> 00:19:00.041
In the morning,

00:19:00.938 --> 00:19:02.263
thank God for the morning,

00:19:02.999 --> 00:19:06.008
I bumped into Stuart and asked his opinion on the shelters.

00:19:06.341 --> 00:19:07.229
I don't like shelters.

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.462
They remind me of prison too much.

00:19:09.462 --> 00:19:11.213
The attitude,

00:19:11.213 --> 00:19:12.904
the atmosphere,

00:19:12.904 --> 00:19:13.404
It's the same thing as prison.

00:19:15.141 --> 00:19:16.002
Couple nights later,

00:19:16.402 --> 00:19:18.884
I began puking and had explosive diarrhea.

00:19:19.384 --> 00:19:21.826
The lady at the desk nodded like she'd seen this before,

00:19:22.146 --> 00:19:23.887
and checked me into emergency right away.

00:19:25.569 --> 00:19:26.069
It's disgusting.

00:19:35.815 --> 00:19:36.656
Fucking disgusting.

00:19:39.838 --> 00:19:40.619
I feel like shit.

00:19:43.921 --> 00:19:49.202
At the homeless shelter there's always the token guy that keeps everybody up all night shitting,

00:19:49.843 --> 00:19:50.363
vomiting,

00:19:52.003 --> 00:19:52.503
coughing,

00:19:52.663 --> 00:19:53.065
horking,

00:19:53.065 --> 00:19:54.044
and smiting.

00:19:56.905 --> 00:19:58.665
Well last night at the shelter I was that guy.

00:20:00.286 --> 00:20:03.766
When you're that guy you don't really care about keeping other people up,

00:20:03.767 --> 00:20:05.307
all you care about is feeling better.

00:20:07.427 --> 00:20:09.268
It really brings things into perspective.

00:20:10.208 --> 00:20:11.249
The doctor took forever.

00:20:12.209 --> 00:20:12.929
When he did arrive,

00:20:13.209 --> 00:20:14.150
He had bad news.

00:20:15.091 --> 00:20:17.272
I had a severe case of gastroenteritis,

00:20:18.293 --> 00:20:21.896
a viral infection causing inflammation in the stomach and intestines.

00:20:23.357 --> 00:20:24.658
Symptoms include diarrhea,

00:20:25.318 --> 00:20:25.819
vomiting,

00:20:25.999 --> 00:20:26.499
headache,

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:27.280
fever,

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:28.901
and abdominal cramps.

00:20:29.602 --> 00:20:30.683
He gave me some codeine,

00:20:31.003 --> 00:20:32.184
a whack load of T3s,

00:20:32.244 --> 00:20:33.124
and sent me on my way.

00:20:42.449 --> 00:20:57.557
I need to find shit to make my bed because I'm not going back to the emergency shelter the doctor told me I can get even more sick and I'm not getting more sick so I'm sleeping on the street from here on in and I'm trying to find shit with

00:20:57.593 --> 00:20:58.097
this,

00:20:59.014 --> 00:21:04.056
trying to find ancient bedding with this wonderful music in the background what is this shit?

00:21:04.056 --> 00:21:08.823
this is kinda weird holy fuck holy shit,

00:21:08.836 --> 00:21:10.097
there's a fucking rat in there,

00:21:10.097 --> 00:21:11.104
that's disgusting

00:21:14.674 --> 00:21:18.168
This will be great for sleeping on.

00:21:20.689 --> 00:21:21.456
Some cardboard.

00:21:24.157 --> 00:21:24.777
Jackpot.

00:21:30.513 --> 00:21:31.719
Does it have all the wheels too?

00:21:33.155 --> 00:21:33.859
Well kind of.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.000
Yeah that's the catch.

00:21:59.518 --> 00:22:00.024
Oh,

00:22:00.344 --> 00:22:00.844
yes.

00:22:07.407 --> 00:22:07.907
Well,

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:10.281
I'm gonna steal this homeless guy's shit.

00:22:11.769 --> 00:22:12.269
Perfect.

00:22:12.409 --> 00:22:13.330
I got my blankets.

00:22:22.974 --> 00:22:23.717
Alright,
well...

00:22:25.275 --> 00:22:26.260
This is where I'm going to bed.

00:22:26.896 --> 00:22:27.641
It's as good as any.

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:42.921
My
stomach hurts.

00:23:43.802 --> 00:23:44.764
I feel bloated.

00:23:45.604 --> 00:23:46.824
I have to go to the washroom.

00:23:48.266 --> 00:23:49.507
This is just gross.

00:23:50.386 --> 00:23:51.728
There's piss all around me.

00:23:52.807 --> 00:23:55.226
There's junkies everywhere.

00:23:55.366 --> 00:23:56.188
I want to get out of here.

00:23:56.227 --> 00:24:00.710
I'm going to go find a nice place where I can actually get some sleep.

00:24:00.869 --> 00:24:03.271
This is too gross.

00:24:03.431 --> 00:24:04.232
I can't sleep here.

00:24:08.073 --> 00:24:09.214
Because I felt so sick,

00:24:09.534 --> 00:24:10.595
I had no appetite.

00:24:11.334 --> 00:24:12.235
This made things easy.

00:24:12.255 --> 00:24:15.676
That is until the clouds rolled in with the Vancouver rain.

00:24:17.477 --> 00:24:19.019
I couldn't find a good spot on the cover.

00:24:19.778 --> 00:24:20.980
I just wanted to sleep.

00:24:26.516 --> 00:24:27.163
Oh,
look at that.

00:24:29.324 --> 00:24:32.366
It's like the fucking jackpot of emergency shelter.

00:24:32.367 --> 00:24:33.341
It looks like a cave.

00:24:33.801 --> 00:24:35.568
And it looks like we have a visitor as well.

00:24:35.903 --> 00:24:36.463
Another,

00:24:38.165 --> 00:24:38.685
Obviously...

00:24:39.827 --> 00:24:43.389
This is the residence of homeless person X and Y.

00:24:43.650 --> 00:24:44.670
So,

00:24:44.670 --> 00:24:45.690
time to be Zed.

00:24:46.893 --> 00:24:47.411
I'm gonna...

00:24:47.513 --> 00:24:47.852
Look at this,

00:24:47.852 --> 00:24:48.412
this is like,

00:24:49.329 --> 00:24:50.316
this is like too good.

00:24:50.933 --> 00:24:52.338
It looks contrived.

00:24:53.519 --> 00:24:54.020
Fuck it.

00:25:25.382 --> 00:25:28.404
It was Christmas Eve and all I wanted was a bed to sleep on,

00:25:28.923 --> 00:25:29.585
so I cheated.

00:25:30.103 --> 00:25:30.626
On a prayer,

00:25:30.744 --> 00:25:33.388
I went to the Yukon shelter and somehow got a room.

00:25:33.825 --> 00:25:34.328
Yes,

00:25:34.565 --> 00:25:35.830
an entire room.

00:25:36.345 --> 00:25:38.052
The sleep was simply glorious.

00:25:38.946 --> 00:25:39.813
When the morning came,

00:25:39.926 --> 00:25:40.854
I cleaned myself up,

00:25:41.127 --> 00:25:41.955
went downstairs,

00:25:42.367 --> 00:25:43.096
and what do you know?

00:25:43.628 --> 00:25:45.377
Santa gives presents to the homeless too.

00:25:46.268 --> 00:25:48.179
All of these presents came from local charities,

00:25:48.449 --> 00:25:49.540
so it's time to cash in.

00:25:55.132 --> 00:25:56.434
Looks like a nice jacket too.

00:25:56.435 --> 00:25:57.436
That looks like a nice fleece.

00:25:57.617 --> 00:25:58.117
Yeah.

00:26:01.223 --> 00:26:01.524
Yeah,
I think so.

00:26:01.524 --> 00:26:01.804
Perfect.
Steve,

00:26:01.804 --> 00:26:02.364
you got something to say?

00:26:02.904 --> 00:26:03.785
I scored an extra goal,

00:26:03.785 --> 00:26:05.805
an extra pair of pants,

00:26:05.805 --> 00:26:06.327
and an extra underwear.

00:26:06.327 --> 00:26:07.047
Your bucket is going down there.

00:26:07.907 --> 00:26:09.067
We're going to be loaded today.

00:26:09.467 --> 00:26:12.109
And see this beautiful thing right here?

00:26:12.110 --> 00:26:12.769
It doesn't fit him.

00:26:13.029 --> 00:26:13.729
It doesn't fit me,

00:26:13.730 --> 00:26:15.710
so I'm going to have to sell it.

00:26:15.711 --> 00:26:18.812
And sponsor my little habit.

00:26:18.932 --> 00:26:22.114
And the retail price is one 10-rock for one jacket.

00:26:22.650 --> 00:26:23.150
So no,

00:26:23.210 --> 00:26:25.511
I'm not in favor of just throwing money at them.

00:26:25.791 --> 00:26:27.591
If we get too generous about this,

00:26:28.111 --> 00:26:32.152
we create ecological niches that actually compel them to this kind of life.

00:26:33.112 --> 00:26:37.834
So all those people who have bleeding hearts and say people really have no choice,

00:26:38.114 --> 00:26:42.775
they are born in a certain socioeconomic class and that determines where they will end up,

00:26:43.035 --> 00:26:47.956
should remind themselves that that also commits them to saying an incentive structure that makes it easy

00:26:47.996 --> 00:26:53.222
to become a bum determines that these people will make those bad decisions.

00:26:53.302 --> 00:26:56.967
You guys think most of these guys spent their Christmas gifts on crack?

00:26:57.287 --> 00:26:57.688
No,

00:26:57.688 --> 00:26:58.829
I think,
0:26:58.909,0:26:49.470
I'm Steven,

00:26:59.710 --> 00:27:02.894
I think all of those guys did.

00:27:02.974 --> 00:27:04.435
Do you think they do it every Christmas?

00:27:04.436 --> 00:27:05.156
I think every year,

00:27:05.256 --> 00:27:05.756
yeah.

00:27:05.796 --> 00:27:07.278
Most of them or not all though?

00:27:07.278 --> 00:27:07.898
Birthdays,

00:27:08.037 --> 00:27:08.538
Christmas.

00:27:08.698 --> 00:27:09.580
I think most of them,

00:27:09.618 --> 00:27:09.919
yeah.

00:27:09.919 --> 00:27:15.664
And I think that's the only reason we're really happy right now is because if the four of us were walking over the bridge and we had no drugs,

00:27:15.664 --> 00:27:16.103
no money,

00:27:16.103 --> 00:27:17.846
and no merchandise to sell,

00:27:17.944 --> 00:27:18.867
we wouldn't be this happy.

00:27:18.985 --> 00:27:19.828
We wouldn't be filming.

00:27:20.246 --> 00:27:23.209
One of us would probably be trying to save the other from jumping off this bridge.

00:27:23.209 --> 00:27:25.213
That's the way it is.

00:27:27.058 --> 00:27:31.301
There's not a lot of legitimate opportunities for people to make money sometimes,

00:27:31.321 --> 00:27:35.764
and of course there's a shadow economy or a street economy that operates all around this.

